BT 1 0 0 1 36 550 Tm (For each candidate CR, integrate its fitted SM resonance tails over the actual SR bins and sum across its resonances and eras. Rank the CRs by predicted) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 536 Tm (resonance yield. Use the smallest set of one or two CRs covering at least 95% of that yield, as recorded in the mass table. Continuum events do not enter) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 522 Tm (this ranking.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 499 Tm (Validation of the CR-selection threshold. The 95% requirement is an operational choice intended to retain nearly all predicted SM resonance tails while) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 485 Tm (limiting the number of control regions. It has no confidence-level interpretation and has not been statistically optimised. The remaining fraction is relative to) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 471 Tm (the resonant contribution alone and does not directly bound the impact on the fitted signal or limits. Validate this choice by adding the next-ranked CR and) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 457 Tm (comparing the fitted signal strength and limits, especially at masses where the selected CR set changes. This stability test remains to be performed.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 434 Tm (Each era contributes one SR channel and one channel for each selected CR. Their binned Poisson likelihoods use expected counts integrated over the) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 420 Tm (original bins. At 0.5 GeV the selected light and charmonium CRs give 12 channels in total. At 2.0 GeV charmonium alone gives eight. Each observed bin) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 406 Tm (enters once per era.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 383 Tm (A single signal strength r scales the signal in every selected channel and era. The workspace imports the signal shape, yield and ten constrained nuisance) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 369 Tm (parameters from the original signal model: electron ID, reconstruction and trigger, two luminosity terms, electron energy scale and four era-specific resolution) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 355 Tm (terms. Shared nuisance constraints enter once. The original regional signal-rate convention is retained; its absolute normalisation still needs a provenance) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 341 Tm (check.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 318 Tm (Within each era, each SM peak has a common mean and normalisation across its CR and SR tail. The SM means and CR resonance and continuum yields) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 304 Tm (float. Widths, tails and CR continuum shape parameters are fixed at their adopted prefit values. Their prefit uncertainties are not propagated. The SR) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 290 Tm (continuum shape is profiled.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 267 Tm (The baseline limit scan uses a positive degree-six Chebyshev continuum with value matching of the nonresonant density at shared edges. The later envelope) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 253 Tm (tests use value matching of the total physical event density at actual SR/CR contacts. Neither fit matches across gaps. The slope is free. This distinction) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 239 Tm (matters when interpreting the baseline limits alongside the bias tests.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 216 Tm (Baseline Combine settings: AsymptoticLimits, Significance and FitDiagnostics use minimizer strategy 0 and MINIMIZER_freezeDisassociatedParams.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 202 Tm (FitDiagnostics additionally uses robustFit 1, saves shapes and normalisations, keeps failures and allows r from -30 to +30. Toy fits use their own) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 188 Tm (configuration.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 800.44 18 Tm (3) Tj T* ET
 

