.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 563 Tm (The injected-signal bias study measures the average displacement of the fitted signal strength. Coverage tests a different property of the) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 546 Tm (inference procedure: how often it retains the true injected signal among the values allowed by a nominal 95% CLs exclusion test. A biased point) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 529 Tm (estimate can coexist with adequate coverage.) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 500 Tm (At each of the 16 masses from 1.2 to 2.7 GeV, we inject a known signal strength equal to the previously calculated median expected limit at) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 483 Tm (that mass. This probes an intensity near the analysis sensitivity. We generate 200 toys with C4 and 200 with L4, for 6400 toys in total. The) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 466 Tm (existing 400 toys at 1.4 GeV are reused.) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 437 Tm (The toys use the saved generator snapshots and the GenerateOnly frequentist-toy configuration. Each toy is analysed with the simultaneous) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 420 Tm (SR plus selected CR model and the shared C4+L4 envelope index profiled across the four eras. The trigger-efficiency nuisance is profiled with) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 403 Tm (its measured constraint. Both branches have the same parameter penalty. Common-boundary C0 relations follow the selected branch,) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 386 Tm (including the CR continuum normalisation at 1.2 and 1.3 GeV.) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 357 Tm (Combine AsymptoticLimits --singlePoint evaluates CLs at the injected r, using minimizer strategy 0 and) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 340 Tm (MINIMIZER_freezeDisassociatedParams, with rMax = 150. A toy excludes its true injection if CLs < 0.05. The estimated coverage is 1 minus) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 323 Tm (the number of such exclusions divided by 200, calculated separately for every mass and generator.) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 294 Tm (For example, the C4 sample at 1.4 GeV excludes the true injection in 8 of 200 toys. Its coverage estimate is therefore 192/200 = 96%. The bars) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 277 Tm (on the next page are exact two-sided Clopper-Pearson 95% binomial intervals. They quantify finite-toy uncertainty on the coverage estimate.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 260 Tm (These intervals replace the approximate Wilson intervals used in the initial chat update.) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 231 Tm (All 6400 unique seed results are present, with finite CLs in [0,1]. The log scan found no exception, failed-fit or NaN messages. These output) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 214 Tm (and log checks do not prove that every conditional minimisation found its global minimum. The two boundary workspaces passed) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 197 Tm (branch-by-branch expected-count and bin-shape comparisons after including the CR normalisation switch.) Tj T* ET
