1 0 0 1 0 0 cm  BT /F1 12 Tf 14.4 TL ET
.090196 .215686 .309804 rg
BT /F2 21 Tf 25.2 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 36 603 Tm (5.4   Goodness of fit in the phi-to-J/psi region) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 13.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 568 Tm (Scope: 16 mass hypotheses, 1.2-2.7 GeV in 0.1 GeV steps, using the adopted C4+L4 envelope and four eras. The signal windows and selected) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 552 Tm (control regions follow the sliding-window table. The fit includes SR and CR data, signal in both, the measured nuisance constraints \(including trigger) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 536 Tm (efficiency\), and the existing total-density C0 relations at actual common boundaries.) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 13.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 510 Tm (The signal strength r is free in the fit. A shared discrete index chooses C4 or L4, and the continuous nuisance parameters are profiled. This study uses) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 494 Tm (the existing workspace parameter ranges; it does not impose an additional r range on the GoF command.) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 13.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 468 Tm (Why evaluate the SR separately? A global SR+CR goodness-of-fit statistic also tests the CR shapes, including the charmonium description. To) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 452 Tm (examine the SR while retaining the constraints provided by the CR data, all channel masks are set to zero during minimisation, and only the CR) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 436 Tm (masks are set to one when Combine evaluates the statistic. The same mask protocol is used for the observed data and for every toy.) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 13.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 410 Tm (Implementation: native Combine GoodnessOfFit with --algo saturated and --cminDefaultMinimizerStrategy 0, using --setParametersForFit for all) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 394 Tm (masks = 0 and --setParametersForEval for CR masks = 1, SR masks = 0. These settings apply to both nominal and saturated-model stages. This is) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 378 Tm (the native masked saturated-likelihood statistic, not a manually calculated Pearson chi-square; shared auxiliary-constraint handling remains that of) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 362 Tm (Combine.) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 13.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 336 Tm (Calibration: 500 frequentist toys per mass, generated and analysed with -t 1 --toysFreq -s SEED. Each toy runs as its own Condor job and) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 320 Tm (immediately saves a result and exit receipt. The seeds are unique: 91000000 + 1000*i + j, with i = 12,...,27 and j = 0,...,499. All 8000 results are) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 304 Tm (present and finite; the observed statistic is calculated once per mass without the toy-generation options.) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 13.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 278 Tm (The p-value is k/500, where k counts toys with a statistic greater than or equal to the observed value. Error bars are exact two-sided Clopper-Pearson) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 262 Tm (95% binomial intervals, describing finite-toy precision. The 0.05 reference is a local diagnostic threshold. Overlapping windows make the 16 tests) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 246 Tm (correlated; no global multiple-testing calibration is claimed.) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 11.5 Tf 13.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 220 Tm (Reproduction: scan_261106/gof_sr_only builds the masked workspaces and evaluates observed statistics; gof_sr_single_toy contains the per-toy) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 204 Tm (runner and full seed manifest. The standalone report script rebuilds the plot and CSV. This GoF tests SR agreement under a simultaneous fit; it does) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 188 Tm (not establish CR adequacy, coverage, or absence of signal-estimator bias. Output completeness alone is not an independent global-minimum audit.) Tj T* ET
.133333 .215686 .266667 rg
BT /F1 9 Tf 10.8 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 20 Tm (Updated 10 November 2026 | Xee analysis) Tj T* ET
