BT /F1 10.5 Tf 12.6 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 513 Tm (C0 enforces equal physical event density at the boundary; C1 would also enforce equal slope. For a common event selection and no physical threshold at that) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 499 Tm (boundary, a kink is a modelling approximation rather than an expected physical feature. Fixing the CR continuum shape makes C1 a potentially strong transfer of its) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 38 485 Tm (local slope into the SR.) Tj T* ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 13.2 TL ET
